{
  "tool_analysis": "# Tool Analysis: Magento Customer Search & Filter\n\n## Step Analysis\nThe recorded steps demonstrate a comprehensive customer management interface in Magento admin with extensive filtering capabilities. The agent successfully demonstrated:\n\n1. **Basic Search Filters**: Name, Email, Customer Group, ZIP, Country, State\n2. **Advanced Filters**: ID range, Customer Since date range\n3. **Grid Controls**: Sorting, Pagination (View per page), Export\n4. **Bulk Operations**: Selection controls, Bulk actions (assign customer group)\n5. **Combined Filtering**: Multiple criteria simultaneously (e.g., VIP Members in California)\n\n## Task Definition\nCreate a reusable tool for searching and filtering customers in Magento admin with parameterized inputs for all available filter criteria. The tool should allow users to:\n- Search by name, email, telephone\n- Filter by customer group, location (ZIP, country, state)\n- Apply ID range and registration date filters\n- Sort results by any column\n- Control pagination (records per page)\n- Export filtered results\n- Perform bulk actions on selected customers\n\n## Action Plan\n1. Navigate to customer management page\n2. Apply name filter (if provided)\n3. Apply email filter (if provided)\n4. Apply customer group filter (if provided)\n5. Apply ZIP filter (if provided)\n6. Apply country filter (if provided)\n7. Apply state filter (if provided)\n8. Apply ID range filters (if provided)\n9. Apply date range filters (if provided)\n10. Apply sorting (if specified)\n11. Set pagination (records per page)\n12. Execute search\n13. Extract results\n14. Optionally perform export or bulk actions\n\n## Variable Identification\nBased on the demonstrated interactions and form field analysis:\n- **Search fields**: name, email, telephone (all optional)\n- **Dropdown filters**: group, country, website (all optional)\n- **Location filters**: ZIP, state (optional)\n- **Range filters**: ID (from/to), customer since (from/to) (optional)\n- **Grid controls**: sort field, sort direction, limit (records per page)\n- **Export format**: CSV, Excel, XML (optional)\n- **Bulk actions**: action type, group assignment (optional)\n\n## Step Optimization\nThe tool will use deterministic steps with elementHash values captured during demonstration. All filter interactions are independent and can be applied in any combination. The search button is clicked after all filters are set. Export and bulk actions are separate optional steps that can be added after filtering.\n\n**Note**: The agent is already logged in when using this tool, so no authentication steps are needed.",
